  "question": {
    "text": "In a meter bridge as shown in the figure, it is given that resistance <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>12.5</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#937;</mi></math> <span style=\"font-size:12px;\"><span style=\"color: rgb(34, 34, 34); font-family: arial, sans-serif;\">&nbsp;</span></span>and that the balance is obtained at a distance <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>39</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cm</mi></math> from end <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi></math> (by jockey <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>J</mi></math>). After interchanging the resistances <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>X</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Y</mi></math>&nbsp;a new balance point is found at a distance <math><msub><mrow><mi>l</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></math> from end <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi></math>. What are the values of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>X</mi></math> (in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#937;</mi></math><span style=\"color: rgb(34, 34, 34); font-family: arial, sans-serif; font-size: 14px;\">)&nbsp;</span>and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>l</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>?<mrow><mn></mn></mrow><br /><br /><img src=\"assets\\qt0305_4a27e6c3f6c6.png\" style=\"width: 370px; height: 224px;\" />&nbsp; &nbsp;"
  },
